ay changing the past isn't like erasuring words on a paper, but adding a lack of correction fluid and after writting new words. The old words haven't disapiared really but they are under the correction fluid. That is the reason I say changing the past is a illusion.<br /> <br /> Other matter Earth isn't spining around the sun, but also is spinning arout the galaxy. That means the planets are moving like springs. To travel to the time you also need inteplanetary vehicles.<br /> <br /> In gothic-punk urban fantasy we could find another surprise, like the time-travelers can't change really the past because reality is controlled by god-machine or the archons and lictors from &quot;Kult: lost divinty&quot;, or changes in the time travel wouldnot affect the original timeline, but a Ucrony with side effects, like vampires ruling the world, or faes stopping industrial revolution, or tribal werebeasts fighing againts aliens from space or robots from a hipotetical future. We could find a multiverse with the factions of Adventure!-Aberrant-Trinity, and empires trying to send agents to controll the powers of more primitive earths.<br /> <br /> * Have you listened anything about the Spanish serie &quot;El ministerio del tiempo&quot; ( = the time ministery), the poor brother of Doctor Who?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","v