vampires ruling the world, or faes stopping industrial revolution, or tribal werebeasts fighing againts aliens from space or robots from a hipotetical future. We could find a multiverse with the factions of Adventure!-Aberrant-Trinity, and empires trying to send agents to controll the powers of more primitive earths.<br /> <br /> * Have you listened anything about the Spanish serie &quot;El ministerio del tiempo&quot; ( = the time ministery), the poor brother of Doctor Who?</div> </div> </div> </div>i havent seen El Misterio Del Tiempo. Primera vez que oigo de el.<br /> <br /> what i was thinking was to throw them on the western setting. make them slowly figure things out, having new allies (Perhaps include the croatoans), making the players aware of the situation with this tribe, knowing that They have To Die and no being able to change it.<br /> <br /> I was thinking of making them arrive to this Disjointed timeline in which pentex already arrived along with the Fomori Leader of my game. Who managed to become the US president, using knowledge of the future and technology but now knowing if the players are in an alternative timeline or if they completely rewritte history","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T12:03:41-07:00","id":980368,"title":"","content":"Maybe a ritual that has them experience past lives all assassins Creed style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T12:09:48-07:00","id":980375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/978842-is-time-travel-possible?p=980366#post980366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> perhaps, but i was thinking about going Alternative Timeline and Fixed points in time</div> </div> </div> </div>If you aren't going for changing the present then you don't have a problem. Run the story you want in the wild west and don't worry about the bigger metaphysical implications.<br /> <br /> There are a few different ways that's possible. Past Lives are one, as mentioned. Umbral Realms and Mirror Zone are another. Either could be indistinguishable from reality to the characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T19:36:14-07:00","id":980530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/978842-is-time-travel-possible?p=979328#post979328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shattered dreams I believe has exactly that. Haven't really read through my copy yet as I just got it. I'm betting someone else here might know. Maybe bunyip.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure does! Bunyip wrote a cracking story / chronicle framework about fixing the past (well, as much as it *can* be. This is WtA, after all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T19:38:35-07:00","id":980532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NateD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/978842-is-time-travel-possible?p=980530#post980530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure does! Bunyip wrote a cracking story / chronicle framework about fixing the past (well, as much as it *can* be. This is WtA, after all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I haven't read that part yet. My wife was excited about were bats so its been all war of rage 2 and more changing breeds 20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T23:46:07-07:00","id":980608,"title":"","content":"Have you seen the mini-serie &quot;Lost if Austen&quot;? A woman who travels to her favorite book &quot;Love and Predjudice&quot; and inadvertenly she changes the story. <br /> <br /> Other suggestion is to use a fictional world like Scarrend Land (atompunk version) to create a campaings about time travels and rival empires tring to invade another worlds ( V the visitors vs Terminator: regenesis). <br /> <br /> In my setting there are different &quot;uchronies&quot; watched and protected by garous and fera, for example a post-apocalipsis alternate future where the bone gnawers are the survivor lords, or a prehistoric age where the red talons don't allow intruders. <br /> <br /> Also other idea is when timeline is changed by time-travelers or chronoauts, the previous timeline really doesn't disappear, but only become a demiplane (where fays are the lords), and those demiplanes can be utopies or distopias. Let's imagine &quot;Brave New World&quot; create a planar gate to travel to &quot;1984&quot;, but cold war between two worlds are stopped by a zombie apocalypse from a third world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T00:16:15-07:00","id":983195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/978842-is-time-travel-possible?p=980354#post980354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking about time paradoxes while I was creating a fanfic about zombie apocalypse and time travels, and my teory is changing details of the past cause &quot;Sch\u00f6ringer's effects&quot;. If you change the past to save a cat's life, then the cat will be alive and dead at same time, but (almost) nobody will notice it. Everybody will see a dead cat, but the time traveler will be the one who see the alive cat.<br /> <br /> What if we send a gold ingot is sent to the last day, and two ingots are molten together? Or a robot is programmed to paint a wall in a laboratory for the experiment. The experiment says if the wall is red, then is painted with blue color, if the wall is blue, then is painted with red color. If it is another color, then to radomly choose to paint with red or blue wall. What color would be the wall. Maybe by a &quot;Schoringer effect&quot; the wall would be violet or pupple, because blue and red from different timeline are fused.<br /> <br /> Let's say changing the past isn't like erasuring words on a paper, but adding a lack of correction fluid and after writting new words. The old words haven't disapiared really but they are under the correction fluid. That is the reason I say changing the past is a illusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of this is... basically a very very very roundabout way of hinting at &quot;if you change the past, you end up in an alternate present&quot; under the Everett Model. Except I'm not really sure why you're arbitrarily mashing the outcomes together, they should be perfectly able to propagate into the future in their own right.<br /> <br /> Most naturally, you'd just end up with a wall that's painted either red or blue, depending on which color the wall in that 'layer' started out as. Mashing future timelines together might be possible with Umbral shenaningans... but while you might end up with the <b>wall</b> being a fusion of the two colors, for consistency's sake, you'd also end up mashing together any other changes. Like, say, if someone paid attention to the wall for a split second more because they liked the color, and now they're getting merged with a them that's just <i>one step</i> away from where they are...<br /> <br /> Not pretty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T00:57:43-07:00","id":983209,"title":"","content":"Or maybe the wall is like a holographic picture, you see the red wall, but you walk two steps and then the wall is now blue. A illusion created by a cuantic Sch\u00f6ringer's effect. For a rpg it can be a hook to create new stories, for example a woman survives a traffic accident, but everybody think she is dead, and only her husband believes her. Or a old widow without children starts to receive letters from somebody who says to be her son from future, telling about a zombie apocalipse... and a day, the old lady finds front of her door a baby. The DNA test confirms he is her impossible grandson. With the baby there is a pendrive telling news about the future, but different files tells different futures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T12:24:31-07:00","id":984007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/978842-is-time-travel-possible?p=980338#post980338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i wanted to figure out a way to throw my PCs in the Wyld West . they are currently in the present, but any ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Run it like an extended Shadows by the Firelight (level four Galliard gift) which puts them into a Wyld West era dream where they can interact with everything and everyone. You can always put in doubt whether it really happened or was just a dream. Perhaps stage it at some long lost Uktena caern and somebody (a PC or an NPC who travels with them) accidentally activates it. Whether they really did travel into the past, or if it was just a dream should be unknowable.<br /> <br /> That gives you the benefits of telling a story in the past with modern characters, yet not having to deal with the issues of time travel paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T18:35:26-07:00","id":984163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/978842-is-time-travel-possible?p=984007#post984007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Run it like an extended Shadows by the Firelight (level four Galliard gift) which puts them into a Wyld West era dream where they can interact with everything and everyone. You can always put in doubt whether it really happened or was just a dream. Perhaps stage it at some long lost Uktena caern and somebody (a PC or an NPC who travels with them) accidentally activates it. Whether they really did travel into the past, or if it was just a dream should be unknowable.<br /> <br /> That gives you the benefits of telling a story in the past with modern characters, yet not having to deal with the issues of time travel paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, run it as a prelude to rediscovering the Caern in the modern day and have the PCs learn how to defeat the bound Wyrm-thing by reliving the events of the initial binding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T07:35:27-07:00","id":984388,"title":"","content":"Other option is characters travel to a dream-memory realm, not the true past... teorically. And when they come back to the present, nothing has changed...or maybe there are some little details, or hallutinations. A example, the hero travels to the past to save his wife, he teorically gets it, but when he comes back to the present, he discover his wife is still dead, by the same cause in the same day....but now the characters meets a woman with same face and personality as his dead wife... coincidence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}